  "note": "Contracts written before E25-S08 introduced EARS classification. Each is a CR2, CR3 or CR4 story whose acceptance criteria describe only the happy path - a real gap, recorded one by one so the list can only shrink, and not a reason to weaken the rule. Repairing one means adding the unwanted-behaviour criterion the contract always needed, which changes a closed contract and therefore needs its own story. The four E25 stories that failed when the rule was tightened after review are deliberately absent: their contracts were repaired instead of baselined, because they were written in the same session as the rule.",
